# The layers in order for a Clone of an enchantment creature under Humility and a later Opalescence. Layer 1: on turn 1
# Clone copies Fear of Missing Out, a {1}{R} 2/3 enchantment creature (CR 707.2) - its mana cost and so its mana value of 2
# with the rest (CR 613.2c). Humility arrives on turn 3, Opalescence on turn 5. Layer 4: Opalescence makes Humility a
# creature (Fear of Missing Out and its copy are enchantments, and creatures already). Layer 6: Humility takes all three
# creatures' abilities. Layer 7b in timestamp order (CR 613.7): Humility's 1/1 first, then Opalescence's mana value - so
# Fear of Missing Out is 2/2, the Clone 2/2 too (its copied mana value; Clone's own {3}{U} would make it 4/4), and Humility
# 4/4. On turn 3, before Opalescence, all were Humility's 1/1. The enters triggers of turn 1 ("discard a card, then draw a
# card") each had Bot1 discard an Island.

